result.overall:
Most of the ledger's per-op numbers check out against out/optables.json, prefill/rows.json, ops1/rows.json and moe/README.md. These reproduce:
- the model step (532.9 ms) and family shares;
- the O1 numbers (443.2 ms, +20.2% at 16K, +23.5% at 64K);
- the per-op derates and in-step kernel times;
- the FI standalone 2649.3 / 1254.2 us and the 1.973 ms link floor;
- the KDA, sparse-MLA and indexer standalone values;
- the calibrated.json 719.4 ms / 22.77K.

The ledger also correctly flags MegaMoE, the MXFP8 KDA projections and the MXFP8 shared GEMMs as new kernels under nvfp4, and treats all other components as unchanged-kernel transfers.

Main problems:
1. Bookkeeping. The item model values sum to 540.3 ms, not 532.9: the 75.1 ms bucket should be about 66.2 ms, and gate_mul is counted twice. The item projected values sum to 854.6 ms, not 847.
2. The headline 847 ms over-projects. A better anchor is the MEASURED release NVFP4-MoE arm at F16K (1063.3 ms) with only the BF16 to MXFP8 GEMM families swapped. That gives about 824 ms (800-857), roughly 19.9K tok/s/GPU, and agrees with the ledger's own bias-corrected 825.
3. The vendored MegaMoE estimate (292 ms) depends on which attribution is used: 207.31 ms excl in rows.json vs 233.93 ms in p3g.attr.txt. The honest range is 281-358 ms. The 8K sub-call is forced by the vLLM-mode workspace cap, not an optional lever.
4. Two proposed fusions target the wrong kernel: the FP8 Q quant belongs after w_uk + RoPE, and gate_mul after w_uv.
5. The MXFP8 in_proj high bound comes from an unaligned-N bench artifact.

Rule compliance is otherwise fine: exact top-k with an exact fallback, BF16 combine and FP4 dispatch, FP32 KDA state, no env toggles.

Items the ledger misses:
- the release arm shows F8K = F16K throughput (15,401 vs 15,409 tok/s/GPU);
- the model underestimates measured weight memory by about 18%;
- DP-rank context imbalance in DEP16 lock-step;
- an unidentified CuTe prologue kernel;
- O1's KDA CTA-halving and state-dependency costs;
- the interaction between removing FI staging and the shared-expert overlap;
- nvfp4 weight-loading and accuracy (gsm8k) bring-up as prerequisites.

Sources (all under /Users/weizha/k31vr-dev/perf-model): out/optables.json, out/prefill.json, out/calibrated.json, microbench/RESULTS.md, microbench/results/prefill/rows.json, microbench/results/prefill/README.md, microbench/results/prefill/analysis/p3g.attr.txt, microbench/results/moe/README.md, microbench/results/ops1/rows.json.
